-Crypto primitives enter as named axioms in `Zkpc.Assumptions` and nowhere else.
+Cryptography is idealized, not axiomatized: `Zkpc.Assumptions` is a named
+data registry that declares no Lean `axiom`, and the cryptographic
+properties enter as restrictions on the symbolic transitions or the ideal
+game views. No real SNARK, signature or encryption scheme is instantiated,
+and the wire-level bridges are open (see `OPEN-PROOFS.md`, "Known gaps").
+The modules are all imported by the umbrella `Zkpc.lean`.
 See `PROVING.md` for the model boundary and contribution rules.
 -/
 
