+tuple in `LedgerSt.acc`. Yet `sweep` pays only tuples in `LedgerSt.acc`
+and `dispute` requires both signals in `LedgerSt.sigs`. Starting from
+`Core.init`, the honest `open'` → `spend` → accepting `redeem` → `sweep`
+sequence therefore pays the gateway nothing, and two emitted conflicting
+tickets are not disputable through `dispute`. The tuple exposes no
+operation that establishes those records. So `flatScheme` is a typing
+exercise only: the T1–T5 guarantees are theorems about `Core.Step`, not
+about executions of this tuple. Closing the gap needs a joint execution
+state with explicit ledger updates, a refinement proof onto `Core.Step`,
+and checked honest-pay and conflicting-pair traces.
